# Proposed features recognized from open_pocket.step by sidecar/import_step.py
# (contract v1 -- see sidecar/CONTRACT.md). Review before use:
# recognition proposes, it does not machine.

# F2: planar, normal +Z, topmost planar face (CHECKLIST row 1.1)
feature F2_Top Plane(z=20.0)

# F4: outer profile under top cap F2: vertical wall loop F4 F6 F8 F14, top at z=20.0, base at z=0.0, material inside the loop; top edge beveled at 90.0deg included with legs that differ edge to edge (F1: 8.0) -- the loop carries 8.0 as its chamfer_depth and its points restate the leg where it changes and 0 where a wall rises to the cap unbeveled (CHECKLIST row 2.2)
# consume with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F4_Profile, comp=control)  [the feature carries its own z + extent]
# the loop is wound CW: material inside, tool outside (the winding convention,
# DECISIONS.md -> "Row-2.4 side selector")
# comp=control is required on Contour runs: recognized boundaries carry rounded
# corners tessellated to chords, and engine comp hard-errors on rounded-corner
# offsets (DECISIONS.md -> "recognized contours propose comp=control")
# the top edge's bevel is 8.0mm deep on most edges, at the included angle the model
# measures, and the loop's points restate the leg where it changes (0 leaves an edge unbroken) --
# break it with: run Form(tool=<ChamferMill>, surface=F4_Profile)  [engine comp: control comp cannot
# lift off an unbroken edge, and the deeper leg reaches about a reach's width round each corner]
feature F4_Profile ProfileBoss(z=20.0, extent=20.0, chamfer_depth=8.0, chamfer_angle=90.0
    0.0 0.0
    0.0 40.0 chamfer_depth=0.0
    60.0 40.0
    60.0 0.0
)

# F9: pocket floor at z=14.0; vertical wall loop F12 F5 F18 F23 F22, mouth at z=20.0, depth 6.0, opens upward; the floor runs out onto F1, which falls away from it -- that side is open, the loop drawn straight out past the blank; floor fillet R1.0 (F10 F7 F19 F21 F20) -- the loop is drawn at the walls, the sharp corner; mouth rounded R1.0 (F3 F11 F13 F15 F16) -- proposed as edge_round, the mouth at the round's top (CHECKLIST row 2.7)
# consume with: run Clear(tool=..., profile=F9_Pocket, stepover=...)  [the feature carries its own z + extent]
# or finish with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F9_Pocket, comp=control)
# comp=control is required on recognized profile Side runs: recognized boundaries carry rounded
# corners tessellated to chords, and engine comp hard-errors on rounded-corner
# offsets (DECISIONS.md -> "recognized contours propose comp=control")
# open toward F1: the floor runs out onto a face that falls away, so
# that side is drawn straight out past the blank, where the engine reads it open;
# everything the loop holds past the floor is air in the model above this floor
# the model has a floor fillet R1.0: the loop is the walls' own line, so a flat
# endmill cuts the corner square, past the model; an endmill with that corner
# radius leaves the fillet
# break the mouth with: run Form(tool=<CornerRounder>, surface=F9_Pocket)  [its ground arc must be R1.0]
feature F9_Pocket ProfilePocket(z=20.0, extent=6.0, edge_round=1.0
    -0.02 8.0
    40.0 8.0
    40.603 8.036
    41.197 8.145
    41.773 8.325
    42.324 8.573
    42.84 8.885
    43.316 9.257
    43.743 9.684
    44.115 10.16
    44.427 10.676
    44.675 11.227
    44.855 11.803
    44.964 12.397
    45.0 13.0
    45.0 27.0
    44.964 27.603
    44.855 28.197
    44.675 28.773
    44.427 29.324
    44.115 29.84
    43.743 30.316
    43.316 30.743
    42.84 31.115
    42.324 31.427
    41.773 31.675
    41.197 31.855
    40.603 31.964
    40.0 32.0
    -0.02 32.0
)
